No — raising the pool size would just delay the same failure. The real bug is in `withClient` (db.js:11-16): `client.release()` only runs if `fn(client)` succeeds. Any query that throws leaks that connection permanently. That matches the log: idle stays at 0 the whole hour while waiting climbs steadily (7→28) — connections are being checked out and never returned, not just contended.

